<!--
Phase 3 output of system-dissector. Captures the Architecture Decision
Records (ADRs) **observed** in the target system. These are decisions
the *original* authors made. The audit is downstream-neutral — what
matters here is fidelity to the source.

Format: MADR 4.0 (https://adr.github.io/madr/). One ADR per top-level
section; number sequentially. Status values: proposed | accepted |
deprecated | superseded by <id>.

Goal: feed Phase 5 HANDOFF (`handoff/decisions.md`) with the *why*
behind the *what*. Porting/integrating without ADRs means porting the
code without the constraints — guaranteed regression.
-->

## Como usar este documento

- **Audience**: tech lead explicando trade-offs ao time que vai
  implementar, portar, ou fazer fork.
- **Next action**: antes de escrever qualquer
  `handoff/implementation-guide.md` para um componente Tier 1, ler os
  ADRs do componente-alvo.
- **Quando re-verificar**: quando o sistema-alvo anuncia breaking change,
  ou quando devs proporem reescrever lógica portada.

## Evidence

- **Overall status**: `verified` | `estimated` | `mixed` *(pick one)*
- **Probe commands**: `<e.g. rg "TODO|FIXME|@deprecated|@see ADR" repo/, git log --grep="ADR-">` [verified|estimated]
- **Last audit**: `<YYYY-MM-DD>`

