## Notes for downstream integrators

- **Critical invariants**: list the ADRs whose outcomes are *inviolable*
  constraints for any port. E.g. "ADR-005 mandates idempotency keys on
  all write endpoints — any port without this is wrong".
- **Open questions**: list ADRs that the original team marked `proposed`
  or where the rationale is thin. These are *your* decisions to make
  when porting.
- **Superseded history**: if `git log` shows an ADR was reverted or
  superseded, capture that here — don't inherit the bad decision.

## Cross-references

- `wiki/architecture.md` — what was built
- `wiki/modules.md` — where each decision manifests in code
- `extract/components.md` — which components each ADR constrains
- `risk-raw.md` — risks tied to specific ADR outcomes (e.g. "ADR-007
  chose SQLite for simplicity — risk under heavy write contention")
- `handoff/decisions.md` — copy/handoff version of these ADRs for the
  implementing team (Phase 5 artifact)
- `<downstream skill:port-plan path>` — opt-in port plan specific to a
  particular destination stack